<article class="env-lemma" id="081K">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/081K">Lemma <span data-tag="081K">37.19.1</span>.</a> Let $f : Y \to X$ be a smooth morphism of schemes. Let $\mathcal{A}$ be a quasi-coherent sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-algebras. The integral closure of $\mathcal{O}_ Y$ in $f^*\mathcal{A}$ is equal to $f^*\mathcal{A}'$ where $\mathcal{A}' \subset \mathcal{A}$ is the integral closure of $\mathcal{O}_ X$ in $\mathcal{A}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a translation of Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/03GG" data-tag="03GG">10.147.4</a> into the language of schemes. Details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>